      "headword": "खुलो",
      "romanization": "khulo",
      "gloss": "open",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:0b3c22e75c0e5a95",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say to open, खोलणो. Then a house and a shop."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: खुलो",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "खुलो — khulo — \"open\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "घर खुलो है। ghar khulo hai. — The house is open."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "खुलो (khulo) is inherited: CDIAL lists Old Marwari khulo, \"open\", in the same entry as खोलणो, under a reconstructed khōll, \"to open\" (CDIAL 3945)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "खुलो (khulo) ends like छोरो and changes the same way, to agree with what is open: घर खुलो (khulo) है।, but दुकान खुली है। (dukān khulī hai.), the shop is open."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "khulo",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *khulo*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "दुकान आज खुली है? — dukān āj khulī hai? — Is the shop open today?",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: **दुकान आज खुली है?** — *dukān āj khulī hai?* — Is the shop open today?]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "हां सा, दुकान खुली है। — hā̃ sā, dukān khulī hai. — Yes, the shop is open.",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: **हां सा, दुकान खुली है।** — *hā̃ sā, dukān khulī hai.* — Yes, the shop is open.]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does खुलो (khulo) mean? (\"Open\".) The shop is open? (दुकान खुली है।)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "spoken": true,
              "id": "MW-C164-khulo-type",
              "prompt": "Say the Marwadi for 'open'.",
              "assesses": [
                "MW-LEX-C164-NOTICE164-01"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 10,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "खुलो",
                "khulo"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Right: खुलो (khulo) is 'open'.",
                "incorrect": "'open' is खुलो (khulo)."
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "MW-C164-band",
      "sequence": 10030,
      "title": "बंद (band) — closed",
      "headword": "बंद",
      "romanization": "band",
      "gloss": "closed",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:47be963d94175c95",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the shop is open. Then Monday and Sunday: सोमवार, रविवार."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: बंद",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बंद — band — \"closed\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सोमवार दुकान बंद है। somvār dukān band hai. — On Monday the shop is closed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बंद (band) is a loan, usually traced to Persian band, \"shut, bound\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बंद (band) does not change: घर बंद (band) है।, दुकान बंद (band) है। Its opposite does: खुलो (khulo), खुली."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "band",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *band*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "दुकान बंद है पण घर खुलो है। — dukān band hai paṇ ghar khulo hai. — The shop is closed, but the house is open.",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: **दुकान बंद है पण घर खुलो है।** — *dukān band hai paṇ ghar khulo hai.* — The shop is closed, but the house is open.]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "दुकान आज बंद कोनी। — dukān āj band konī. — The shop isn't closed today.",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: **दुकान आज बंद कोनी।** — *dukān āj band konī.* — The shop isn't closed today.]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does बंद (band) mean? (\"Closed\".) Does it change for a shop? (No.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "spoken": true,
              "id": "MW-C164-band-type",
              "prompt": "Say the Marwadi for 'closed'.",
              "assesses": [
                "MW-LEX-C164-NOTICE164-02"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 10,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "बंद",
                "band"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Right: बंद (band) is 'closed'.",
                "incorrect": "'closed' is बंद (band)."
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
