          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say he comes from the market. Then the shop is closed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: तांई",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तांई — tā̃ī — \"until\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दुकान दिनूगै ६ सूं १० तांई खुली है। dukān dinūgai chha sū̃ das tā̃ī khulī hai. — The shop is open in the morning from six until ten."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सूं opens the stretch of time, and तांई (tā̃ī) closes it. The hours are digits, read as numbers: ६ is chha, १० is das."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तांई (tā̃ī) is probably inherited from Sanskrit tāvat, \"so long\". CDIAL gives no Marwari form in this entry, but it lists an Old Gujarati word for \"up till\" there (CDIAL 5804)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सूं … तांई (tā̃ī) frames any stretch: आथण ५ सूं ८ तांई (tā̃ī), in the evening from five until eight."
            }
          ]
        },
